  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Timor-Leste&#x2019;s Border and Law Enforcement Capacities to Address Trafficking in Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to prioritize the recommendations in the 2021 Trafficking in Persons (TIP) report and contribute to enhancing national capacities to prevent TIP and ensure the effective protection of victims of trafficking in Timor-Leste. This will be achieved through ensuring that the institutional prevention and protection mechanisms are enhanced to combat human trafficking and address emerging trends. The project will ensure that law enforcement officers and border officials have the knowledge and skills to identify, refer and conduct victim-centered human trafficking investigations, enhance implementation of legislation to prevent TIP, and increase awareness to address fraudulent labour recruitment practices and promote safe migration pathways.</narrative>
  </description>
